[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
Kaigi has been installed under %%WWWDIR%%.
See %%DOCSDIR%%/BASELINE.md for source provenance.

Enable and start the independent Kaigi service:
    sysrc kaigi_enable="YES"
    service kaigi start

Configure %%PREFIX%%/etc/kaigi/kaigi.conf, users, meeting-properties.json
and site-translations.json before starting. Protect credentials and TLS keys.
LDAP support is included, disabled by default; configure ldap/ldap.conf and
ldap/group-meetings.json before setting LDAP_ENABLED=true.
MiroTalk may coexist using its own service and settings.
Choose distinct listener addresses or ports when running both services.

See kaigi(8), kaigi.conf(5), kaigi-ldap.conf(5), and
%%DOCSDIR%%/BASELINE.md for the pending release validation gates.
The example fail2ban filter is in %%EXAMPLESDIR%%/fail2ban/kaigi.conf.

Before public deployment, run make corresponding-source and publish the
result at %%KAIGI_SOURCE_URL%%. This target collects the application and
locked npm inputs; inherited RNNoise source/rebuild provenance remains
a separate release gate. Add the matching mediasoup port and complete
Corresponding Source inputs for the actual deployed combination.
EOM
}
]
